Z||000000||fiero56||02-16-2000||10:08 PM||||I was listening to cartalk via realplayer on the 'net tonight, and one question was why the owners manual for new beelte says don't let the engine warm up at idle. They got to talking about something else and never answered that question, just said don't let it warm up at idle.<BR>Why is this? Is it bad to warm up the Fiero before driving it?||||reg||1
Z||000001||fierospeeder||02-16-2000||11:48 PM||||ive heard this before, and i think its because the car uses more fuel and there was some other reason also which i cant remember at this moment.  Your suppose to drive a car slowly for a few miles before drag racing hondas.<P>I own the old 74 beetle so im not those yuppies that think its trendy to own the new ones.  I owned it before the new one came out, like 4 or 5 years ago.  The manuals and books i have on the beetle, say you have to let this car warmup for a few minutes to get the oil circulated and most people just use straight 30w which is preferred.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||fiero56||02-17-2000||06:34 AM||||I usually give my Fiero 5 minutes to warm up before driving off. But this is because if I try to drive it cold, it horribly hessitates and tries to stall. There's a thread about the problem in the archives somewhere.||||reg||1
